'''Dark Aegis Garu''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] event. It was added in [[Version 10.5 Update|Version 10.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 609
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Dark Aegis Garu
|name2 = Dark Beastlord Garu
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark Beastlord Garu''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Dark Aegis Garu is an interesting unit, similar to normal [[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Garu]] like all EPICFEST units are to their UBERFEST counterparts, but still has mostly different usage and an extra [[Special Abilities|ability]] only gained in his Evolved Form.

Dark Aegis Garu is built similarly to Mighty Aegis Garu, being a mid-ranged tank with guaranteed Mini-Waves and an Omni Attack for consistency. However, he also shares many of the same weaknesses: High cost, egregiously long recharge time, a long attack animation and slow movement speed, along with no immunities apart from [[Immune to Waves]] like some other [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]]. What sets Dark Aegis Garu apart, other than his target traits, is that he has one less knockback, giving him better bulk in exchange for survivability, and that he has a 100% Strengthen at 50% HP.

As for general usage, Dark Aegis Garu is built very similarly to [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Maeda Keiji]]. Both are bulky attackers who stand at 320 range, allowing them to hide behind meatshields while still being able to protect backliners, and both have a 100% Strengthen to skyrocket their damage output. The difference is while Dark Aegis Garu has much better HP and noticeably better DPS, alongside pierce from the Mini-Wave and Omni Attack, Keiji has a much better cost and cooldown.

Dark Aegis Garu is also [[Resistant|Tough]] against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies. He is generally a solid tanker against them. Not only can he take a lot of punishment with 612,000 effective HP at Lv.30 against Traitless, but he also packs strong offense. Dark Garu can act as a brick wall against many Traitless enemies, such as [[Dolphina]], [[Master A.]], [[Kory]] and [[Mr. Mer]], and his Wave Immunity supports this. However, several Traitless enemies like [[R.Ost]] are often paired with support from different Traits that could quickly eat away at Dark Aegis Garu's HP, which damages his viability against Traitless. Additionally, Dark Aegis Garu also faces tough competition from [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Dogumaru]], who has less bulk and DPS, but is cheaper and has a much faster cooldown, with his True Form having less than half of Dark Aegis Garu's cooldown, allowing him to be used more flexibly and have a higher defensive uptime.

To get the most out of Dark Aegis Garu's potential, it is strongly recommended to use Catseyes and boost him all the way to Lvl.50, due to his stat-based nature. At Lv.50, he gets a strong 243,000 HP, allowing him to be used much more comfortably as a generalist tank, and alleviates his weakness in mixed stages. This jumps up to a monstrous 972.000 HP against Traitless. Additionally, his damage output gets a big boost, gaining a respectable 12.1K DPS without Strengthen, and an amazing 24.2K DPS with it. While his issues with cost and cooldown remain, a boosted Dark Aegis Garu is a force to be reckoned with.

